    <string name="settings_mpv_helper_text">One mpv option per line (key=value). These apply after the settings above and override them.\n\n• Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored; a lone key (e.g. hr-seek) means yes.\n• Subtitle keys (sub-color, sub-pos, …) also override the app\'s subtitle settings.\n• Do not quote values — they reach mpv as-is, so quotes become part of the value (sub-color=#FF0000 works; sub-color="#FF0000" does not). A # inside a value is fine here.</string>
    <string name="settings_mpv_fonts_helper_text">Fonts: JellyPlay bundles a fallback font plus any font installed in the subtitle settings, and sub-font-provider defaults to none — so system fonts (e.g. Roboto) do not resolve. sub-fonts-dir and sub-font-provider are overridable here: point sub-fonts-dir at a folder this app can read (another app\'s Android/media folder is not accessible under scoped storage).</string>
